{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.SkeinCounterfactual","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinCounterfactual","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationBridge"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.no_scalar_faithful_to_halts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.no_scalar_faithful_to_halts","kind":"theorem","line":375,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinCounterfactual.lean#L375-L386","doc":"**No scalar is faithful to halting POINTWISE (sorry-free).** No\nstate-independent verdict `v` satisfies `∀ P, v ↔ Halts P` on `stallAbove`.\n\n**Scope (a).** This excludes the *pointwise* claim shape only. It does **not**\nexclude a scalar faithful to the universally-quantified statement\n`∀ P, Halts P` — that is trivially inhabited, and it is the shape the corpus\nactually uses. See the module docstring's correction record. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.halts_not_constant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.halts_not_constant","kind":"theorem","line":366,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinCounterfactual.lean#L366-L373","doc":"**`Halts` is not a constant predicate.** Hence, by `const_of_scalar_faithful`,\nno state-independent scalar verdict is equivalent to halting. The obstruction\nroute needs an invariant that varies over states — which a one-dimensional\n`Obs` evaluated at a fixed `q₀` does not supply. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.stallAbove_not_halts_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.stallAbove_not_halts_two","kind":"theorem","line":360,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinCounterfactual.lean#L360-L364","doc":"`2` does not halt under `stallAbove`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.stallAbove_iterate_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.stallAbove_iterate_two","kind":"theorem","line":354,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinCounterfactual.lean#L354-L358","doc":"Every iterate fixes `2`: the stalled orbit never moves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.stallAbove_halts_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.stallAbove_halts_one","kind":"theorem","line":351,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinCounterfactual.lean#L351-L352","doc":"`1` halts under `stallAbove`, in one step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.stallAbove","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.stallAbove","kind":"def","line":344,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinCounterfactual.lean#L344-L349","doc":"Collapse `{0,1}` to the normal form; stall everywhere above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.const_of_scalar_faithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.const_of_scalar_faithful","kind":"theorem","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinCounterfactual.lean#L323-L334","doc":"**A state-independent scalar can only decide a constant predicate.** If a\nsingle truth value `v` (the \"obstruction is non-zero at `q₀`\" verdict, which\ncarries no dependence on the state `P`) is equivalent to `Pred P` for every\n`P`, then `Pred` is constant on states.\n\nThis is the state-indexed form of `ObstructionVerdictCap.verdict_cap`, which\nis the same `Iff` algebra with the quantifier stripped; the two are kept\napart only because that module carries no dependency on this one. See the\nmodule docstring for what this does **not** show. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qCollatzSystem_normalForm_periodic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qCollatzSystem_normalForm_periodic","kind":"theorem","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinCounterfactual.lean#L305-L315","doc":"**The q-Collatz instance discharges the periodicity hypothesis.** Recorded as\na lemma rather than asserted in prose: `attractor_period_two` *is*\n`IsPeriodicPt` at `p = 2`, definitionally. Both prior corrections on this\nbranch were \"asserted about the instance, never checked against it\", so the\ndischarge is machine-checked here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.not_blowsUp_of_halts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.not_blowsUp_of_halts","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinCounterfactual.lean#L293-L301","doc":"**Contrapositive.** A halting orbit never blows up — q-Collatz convergence at\nan orbit gives q-NS regularity at that orbit for free, with an explicit\nbound. The implication is one-directional: bounded complexity does **not**\nimply halting (a bounded orbit may cycle forever without reaching the normal\nform), which is exactly why descent is the harder question. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.not_halts_of_blowsUp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.not_halts_of_blowsUp","kind":"theorem","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinCounterfactual.lean#L278-L291","doc":"**Blow-up excludes halting, within one system.** When the normal form is\nperiodic — as the q-Collatz attractor is, by `attractor_period_two` — an\norbit with unbounded filtration cannot reach it. The boundedness question and\nthe descent question are not independent *of the same instance*.\n\n**Not a cross-leg identification.** `sys` is one system; see the section\nheader. The corpus's two legs are different instances, and on the concrete\nNS instance this hypothesis is unsatisfiable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.regular_of_halts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.regular_of_halts","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinCounterfactual.lean#L259-L276","doc":"**Halting bounds the filtration.** A halting orbit lands in the normal form's\ncycle and thereafter visits only finitely many states, so its complexity\nnever exceeds the maximum over the finite prefix together with the cycle.\nThe bound is explicit and depends on `P` — no uniform bound is claimed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.iterate_mem_cycle_of_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.iterate_mem_cycle_of_ge","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinCounterfactual.lean#L246-L257","doc":"Reaching a **periodic** normal form pins every later state to a point of the\ncycle: past the landing time `k`, the orbit is `step^[i] normalForm` for some\n`i < p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.not_orbit_descent_of_counterexample","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.not_orbit_descent_of_counterexample","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinCounterfactual.lean#L186-L200","doc":"**One counterexample, two walls.** If `P` either blows up or fails to halt,\nthe shared orbit-descent hypothesis (non-increasing, and strictly dropping off\nthe normal form) fails at `P`. A q-NS singularity and a q-Collatz divergent\norbit cannot both be ruled out by one descent lemma — whichever appears first\ndestroys the route to both. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.not_len_nonincreasing_of_blowsUp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.not_len_nonincreasing_of_blowsUp","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinCounterfactual.lean#L168-L177","doc":"**A q-NS blow-up witness refutes every monotone Lyapunov filtration.** If the\norbit of `P` blows up, the filtration cannot be non-increasing along it.\nContrapositive of `regular_of_len_nonincreasing` — the abstract shadow of\n\"bounded enstrophy rules out blow-up\", read backwards: exhibiting a\nsingularity is exactly exhibiting a failure of monotone complexity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.exists_descent_iff_halts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.exists_descent_iff_halts","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinCounterfactual.lean#L152-L164","doc":"**Descent ⟺ halting on the cone.** Combining with `halts_of_len_descent`:\nthe existence of a strict descent measure is not a sufficient condition that\nmight be easier to verify — it carries exactly the conjecture's content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.exists_descent_of_halts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.exists_descent_of_halts","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinCounterfactual.lean#L129-L150","doc":"**The hitting time is a descent measure.** If every element of a\nforward-invariant cone halts, then the step count to the normal form strictly\ndecreases off it — so a descent measure exists. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.not_descent_of_not_halts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinObservationSystem.not_descent_of_not_halts","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinCounterfactual.lean#L88-L99","doc":"**A q-Collatz counterexample refutes every descent measure.** If `P` does not\nhalt, then for every forward-invariant cone `C` containing `P` there is **no**\nstrict `len`-descent off the normal form. Contrapositive of\n`halts_of_len_descent`: the open content of q-Collatz is the *existence* of\nsuch a descent, so a single non-halting orbit destroys every candidate at\nonce — not merely the one being tested. ","signatureChunk":0}]}